{"tool_name":"gcocoa","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"gcocoa","home":"http://biit.cs.ut.ee/gprofiler/gcocoa.cgi","license":"Freeware","summary":"A tool of the g:Profiler web server. It enables to do functional annotation for several gene lists at the same time and compare their results.","addition_date":"2015-01-22T11:13:22Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:01:20.167131Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"version":["1"],"collections":["Elixir-EE","g:Profiler toolkit"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:gcocoa","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"jaak.vilo@ut.ee","name":"Jaak Vilo","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"biit.support@ut.ee","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"ELIXIR-EE","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["API documentation"],"url":"https://biit.cs.ut.ee/gprofiler/help.cgi?help_id=57"},{"type":["General"],"url":"https://biit.cs.ut.ee/gprofiler/page.cgi?welcome"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Identifier","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0842"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Comparison","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2424"},{"term":"Gene functional annotation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3672"},{"term":"Gene-set enrichment analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2436"},{"term":"Statistical calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2238"}]}],"name":"gCocoa","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkw199","metadata":{"abstract":"Functional enrichment analysis is a key step in interpreting gene lists discovered in diverse high-throughput experiments. g:Profiler studies flat and ranked gene lists and finds statistically significant Gene Ontology terms, pathways and other gene function related terms. Translation of hundreds of gene identifiers is another core feature of g:Profiler. Since its first publication in 2007, our web server has become a popular tool of choice among basic and translational researchers. Timeliness is a major advantage of g:Profiler as genome and pathway information is synchronized with the Ensembl database in quarterly updates. g:Profiler supports 213 species including mammals and other vertebrates, plants, insects and fungi. The 2016 update of g:Profiler introduces several novel features. We have added further functional datasets to interpret gene lists, including transcription factor binding site predictions, Mendelian disease annotations, information about protein expression and complexes and gene mappings of human genetic polymorphisms. Besides the interactive web interface, g:Profiler can be accessed in computational pipelines using our R package, Python interface and BioJS component. g:Profiler is freely available at http://biit.cs.ut.ee/gprofiler/.","authors":[{"name":"Adler P."},{"name":"Arak T."},{"name":"Kolberg L."},{"name":"Peterson H."},{"name":"Reimand J."},{"name":"Reisberg S."},{"name":"Vilo J."}],"citationCount":940,"date":"2016-07-08T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"g:Profiler-a web server for functional interpretation of gene lists (2016 update)"},"pmcid":"PMC4987867","pmid":"27098042","type":["Other"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Data identity and mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3345"},{"term":"Data mining","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3473"},{"term":"Function analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_1775"},{"term":"Ontology and terminology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0089"},{"term":"Statistics and probability","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2269"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"gCocoa","home":"https://bio.tools/gcocoa","license":"Freeware","version":"1","summary":"A tool of the g:Profiler web server. It enables to do functional annotation for sev